        "type": "text",
        "text": "That is the real answer. The document's architecture creates a genuine gap I had missed:\n\n- § 1.7 **Services** = *hosted* software + services → gets full-term conformity under § 19.2.\n- § 1.4 **Deliverable** = reports, configurations, integrations, designs → gets ninety days.\n- § 13.2 contemplates **software and Vendor Technology delivered on a paid-up/perpetual basis** — non-hosted software, which gets at best the ninety-day Deliverable period, versus our preferred **12 months for software**.\n\nSo this is a parametric shortfall, not merely a formatting artifact. Let me validate a minimal fix."
      },
      {
        "type": "tool_use",
        "id": "toolu_01LhtFJ1L32MVQRLftGjm6d1",
        "name": "propose_redline",
        "input": {
          "level": "preferred",
          "summary": "Extend the Deliverable conformity period to twelve (12) months for Deliverables consisting of or embedding perpetually/paid-up licensed software or Vendor Technology; keep ninety (90) days for other Deliverables and add numerals.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] Section 19.2 warrants Hosted Services for the full subscription term, but software and Vendor Technology licensed to us on a paid-up or perpetual basis under Section 13.2 is not hosted and so receives only the ninety-day Deliverable period. Our position is twelve months of conformity for software, so we have extended the period for software Deliverables while leaving ninety days for all other Deliverables; we can accept ninety days across the board as a fallback if the software is in practice always delivered hosted.",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "replace",
              "paragraphId": "p0077",
              "oldText": "For ninety days after delivery or acceptance, whichever is later, each Deliverable will materially conform to its documentation and acceptance criteria.",
              "newText": "For ninety (90) days after delivery or acceptance, whichever is later, each Deliverable will materially conform to its documentation and acceptance criteria, provided that for any Deliverable that consists of or embeds software or Vendor Technology licensed to Customer on a paid-up or perpetual basis, that period is twelve (12) months."
            }
